{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nPlaceholder epic for R-4 from the DSO gap analysis (~/dso_rebar_plan_review_gap_report.md, R-4), REFRAMED during design review from 'cite bug history in rubrics' into a first-class, extensible mechanism.\n\nDSO anchors its reviewer prompts with concrete worked examples from its own bug history (e.g. the --label vs --labels flag-mismatch defect; a false-positive from a 20-ticket calibration record). Concrete failures calibrate an LLM reviewer far better than abstract instructions. rebar has a BETTER source than DSO for this: the REVIEW_RESULT sidecar accumulates real per-criterion findings and false-positive signal.\n\n## The concept (converged reframe)\nA CALIBRATION-EXAMPLE LIBRARY for plan review:\n- A CORE set of examples ships with rebar (per criterion: a sharp good/bad worked example).\n- Projects can add their OWN project-specific examples -- mirroring the existing extension seam (.rebar/criteria_routing.json overlay + .rebar/prompts/ overrides). An absent overlay fails open to the core set.\n- This makes rebar LEARN OVER TIME: it increases its effectiveness based on accumulated experience in a SPECIFIC project (a false positive seen once becomes a calibration anchor that prevents its recurrence).\n\nThis is the natural evolution of R-4 + the sidecar's per-criterion FP record + the existing project-overlay architecture.\n\n## Open design questions (for the brainstorm session)\n- [ ] WHERE in the four-pass pipeline is example context injected? (Pass-1 finder rubrics? Pass-2 verifier? both? Injecting into the verifier risks anchoring the FP-filter; injecting into the finder shapes what gets surfaced. Decide deliberately.)\n- [ ] HOW are examples CURATED to prevent unbounded growth? (A per-criterion cap? Relevance/recency scoring? Dedup by norm_id? Promotion from sidecar -> curated library needs a gate so the prompt doesn't bloat and bust the cache.)\n- [ ] Sourcing: hand-authored core vs auto-mined from sidecar corpus vs human-curated promotion of sidecar findings.\n- [ ] Interaction with the CI prompt/routing drift-parity gate and prompt-cache efficiency (examples are prompt weight).\n- [ ] Format/contract: how examples attach to a criterion (prompt front-matter? a sibling examples file keyed by criterion id?).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] This epic holds the reframed concept + open design questions from the review discussion\n- [ ] Sequenced AFTER the G-series rubric enrichments (no point anchoring rubrics about to be rewritten)\n- [ ] Placeholder only pending a dedicated brainstorming session\n- [ ] A decision on injection point(s) in the plan-review pipeline\n- [ ] A curation mechanism with a bounded-growth guarantee\n- [ ] A core example set + a project-extension seam consistent with the existing overlay architecture\n- [ ] A promotion path from observed sidecar findings/FPs into curated examples"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785007134316291001,"uuid":"e65d7596-a40f-4f4e-8bda-00f3a2279a54"}